{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong","id":1475044,"title":"Solar Experience and Charms, what could go wrong?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-20T09:18:59-08:00","id":1475044,"title":"Solar Experience and Charms, what could go wrong?","content":"I've been crunching the numbers and at 300xp, Essence 5, if you spent all of your exp on favored/caste charms that would only yield 37 charms. That seems like a lot but the Dodge charm tree is 27 charms deep, let alone something like Craft of Performance. More realistically, this is only around 5 charms per favored/caste ability which seems pathetic for an Essence 5 Solar.<br /> <br /> On top of that, if you actually took Sorcery or MA or Evocs for your Solar, that could be 20 (figuring 2 solar exp per session, roughly) or so more &quot;powers&quot; than a Solar that didn't want to use those. I think I'd rather have a spell over an ability increase any day of the week therefore, saying a &quot;power&quot; and other uses of Solar Exp imo are not comparable. <br /> <br /> Does it really break the game to let characters use Solar Exp to buy favored/caste charms? What if you treated them as unfavored/non-caste for the price point? IE 10 Solar Exp per charm and ruled that you can't buy unfavored/non-caste charms with Solar Exp?<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-28T13:20:34-08:00","id":1501567,"title":"","content":"*bump*<br /> <br /> But, also I just started making most of the &quot;upgrade&quot; charms and charms with repurchaseable upgrades automatic upgrades when you get to the minimums. Seems much better this way. Also, the Golden Calibration seems to have the same though.<br /> <br /> Tyzerg","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-31T04:21:58-08:00","id":1501800,"title":"","content":"Nothing will &quot;break&quot; by letting players spend Solar XP on charms. I did the same in a game I ran. But I understand why the game writers made the rule.<br /> <br /> Unlike in previous editions, E5 isn't a ate that all the cool charms are locked behind, and E6 isn't a &quot;must have&quot; goal. Getting to E5 in game mechanics terms mainly means that all charms are now available (because meeting ability requirements is far less XP intensive than getting E5). Rather than see it as &quot;I got to E5 and ONLY have this many charms&quot;, look at it as &quot;I achieved the pinnacle of Essence Enlightenment while only needing to learn this many charms&quot;. (I know, E6+ is still a thing, but in Exalted 3rd edition E6+ charms aren't as mega-powerful as in Ex 1-2).<br /> <br /> I also think the writers made the rule to encourage more diverse builds. Solar XP forces more points spent on non-charms, making the characters more well rounded instead of mono-focused.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, if you think Solar XP should be spent on anything without restriction, that's fine. It's kind of like just giving more normal XP, but it just doesn't contribute to raising Essence. *Disclaimer*- Your players may find a way to use the rule change break the game and ruin everything in ways no sane person can anticipate or comprehend. That's what some players do.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/472-keldorn2198","name":"Keldorn2198","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-01T03:17:24-08:00","id":1501860,"title":"","content":"I will not touch the solar XP, for reasons Keldorn wrote above. What I am thinking on doing with the charms is make a discount on the cost based of the comparative level. If you are Essence 4 and want to learn an essence 2 charm, it would be 4-2=2 less xp to learn. Essence 5 and want to learn an essence 1 charm? 5-1= 4 less xp than the table. That way people get more charms, but low level ones, which helps to diversify a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12490-virtud","name":"Virtud","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12490_1.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-01T10:50:25-08:00","id":1501880,"title":"","content":"Looking back at the math here, at 300 XP, you'd have 52 Charms + some number of free Excellencies based on your stats and Charm selections. 37 doesn't account for all your starting Charms.<br /> <br /> Calling that a &quot;pathetic&quot; level of power for an Exalt that just reached the minimum cusp for Essence 5 seems to be severely underestimating how much 52 Solar Charms can do; even with many of the issues in the Solar Charm set. It's also treating Essence 5 like hitting Level 20 in D&amp;D where that's as powerful as you get without using optional rules.<br /> <br /> The differentiation between normal XP and Solar XP is valuable on its own, and if all that power isn't enough (esp. since you can still supplement it with Solar XP in other ways) changing Solar XP isn't really going to fix your problem. A far simpler solution that doesn't mess with any other part of the game? Increase the XP thresholds for increasing Essence. Those numbers are just there to set an arbitrary default pace. Double how much XP it gets to get to Essence 5, and you double how many Solar Charms they're likely to have, as well as significantly increased their time to build up Solar XP for stats/Evocations/spells/etc. for even more potency. If 90 Charms + Excellencies + whatever you spent all your Solar XP on isn't enough to feel appropriately powerful when just hitting Essence 5 (keeping in mind that means you haven't bought any Essence 5 stuff outside of your Supernal Ability yet!), I don't think you're going to be satisfied by just some minor tweaks to the XP system regardless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-01T21:03:44-08:00","id":1501925,"title":"","content":"For perspective, most my games reach E5 and at that point we're regularly tackling stuff much harder than most canon opposition the game has. Playing entire countries against each other as a matter of course, churning artifacts like candy and laughing at 30+ damage decisive attacks. &quot;52 charms&quot; does a hell of a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-02T07:53:29-08:00","id":1501950,"title":"","content":"Maybe 52 charms seems like comparatively little because there are so bonkers many Solar charms? So 52 feels like a drop in the ocean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1631-karthak","name":"Karthak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1631_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-02T12:12:46-08:00","id":1501968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1501880#post1501880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking back at the math here, at 300 XP, you'd have 52 Charms + some number of free Excellencies based on your stats and Charm selections. 37 doesn't account for all your starting Charms.<br /> <br /> Calling that a &quot;pathetic&quot; level of power for an Exalt that just reached the minimum cusp for Essence 5 seems to be severely underestimating how much 52 Solar Charms can do; even with many of the issues in the Solar Charm set. It's also treating Essence 5 like hitting Level 20 in D&amp;D where that's as powerful as you get without using optional rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think I ever said &quot;pathetic&quot; but my point still stands. 52 charms at 300 exp is only 5 charms per favored/caste ability. If you decided to push, let's say Socialize, to the max and put 25 of those charms into it, you'd still have 17 charms to get to just to complete that tree. Then you'd have 3 charms for each of your other 9 caste/favored abilities. So, yes that would be a pathetic amount of charms for the other 9 abilities at Essence 5.<br /> <br /> Also, it seems most people here are treating Essence 5 like it's the &quot;beginning of the actual game&quot; which I feel 60 sessions into a campaign is a lot. Maybe I'm just an old man now, but getting one group to commit to over a year of continuous play of the same campaign is easier said than done. We are just now getting to Essence 3 and it's been almost 2 years of biweekly play.<br /> <br /> I understand that Essence 5 is not the end-all of Exalted power level but for most practical play groups, it's unachievable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1501880#post1501880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The differentiation between normal XP and Solar XP is valuable on its own, and if all that power isn't enough (esp. since you can still supplement it with Solar XP in other ways) changing Solar XP isn't really going to fix your problem. A far simpler solution that doesn't mess with any other part of the game? Increase the XP thresholds for increasing Essence. Those numbers are just there to set an arbitrary default pace. Double how much XP it gets to get to Essence 5, and you double how many Solar Charms they're likely to have, as well as significantly increased their time to build up Solar XP for stats/Evocations/spells/etc. for even more potency. If 90 Charms + Excellencies + whatever you spent all your Solar XP on isn't enough to feel appropriately powerful when just hitting Essence 5 (keeping in mind that means you haven't bought any Essence 5 stuff outside of your Supernal Ability yet!), I don't think you're going to be satisfied by just some minor tweaks to the XP system regardless.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't a bad suggestion at all. I might consider this. My fix so far has been to just allow most Charms that seem to upgrade pre-existing charms to be auto-upgrades for free (such as Perfect Mirror to Flawlessly Impenetrable Disguise) once the minimum requirements are met\u200b. Charms that seem to be minor or specific to certain situations (Sea Ambush Technique for instance) are treated like the extensions of Master Horseman's Technique and are purchased for 2-4exp.<br /> <br /> So far, this has allowed the players to explore the trees of their caste/favored abilities without feeling like they are missing out on cool &quot;tricks&quot; from other trees that aren't worth a full charm purchase. I haven't seen a balance issue yet with it but I'm sure it's also not perfect.<br /> <br /> Tyzerg","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3230,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","user":"Tyzerg","date":". 02-02-2023, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-02T15:31:22-08:00","id":1501989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong#post1475044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More realistically, this is only around 5 charms per favored/caste ability which seems <b>pathetic</b> for an Essence 5 Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1501968#post1501968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think I ever said &quot;pathetic&quot;...</div> </div> </div> </div>Bolded it for you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 52 charms at 300 exp is only 5 charms per favored/caste ability. </div> </div> </div>I think most of us don't really expect this approach to the game where you're trying to evenly spread out Charms between all of your Caste and Favored Abilities.<br /> <br /> I'd also point out that given how fast Solar Charm Ability Minimums jump to 4 and 5, most characters aren't going to qualify for all the many Charms between those 10 Abilities because they're not going to worry about getting them all to 5. Most PCs are probably putting the vast majority of their Charms in 2-4 Abilities, with a small smattering in other places. As well, the Solar Charms are generally ones where exploring every last branch really isn't that important. While there are obvious divisions in some of them, they all have Charm packages that support more specific concepts that mean you don't have to buy every Charm to get what matters to why you picked that Ability as one to focus on.<br /> <br /> With intended groups of 3-6 players, and Solar Charms not really rewarding overlap over diversity, most Charms worth having are going to come up even if one Character doesn't have them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, yes that would be a pathetic amount of charms for the other 9 abilities at Essence 5. </div> </div> </div>Why? Epic heroes aren't pathetic because they can can cut a mountain in half, but can only throw a knife twice as well as any normal human ever could. Specialization is not a bad thing for the game as it's advised to be played.<br /> <br /> Considering the 6-8 dice + 1 Charm + Excellency is enough for a Solar to beat 90-95% of potential challenges in the setting that Ability addresses, you don't need 20+ Charms to be a powerhouse by the standards of Creation, even if you're still far from the pinnacle of Exalted capabilities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, it seems most people here are treating Essence 5 like it's the &quot;beginning of the actual game&quot; which I feel 60 sessions into a campaign is a lot. </div> </div> </div>Eh? I'm treating it as superfluous because by that point a circle of Solars are so powerful you need to beak out every contrived excuse as to why enemies have the power to stand up to them. You're the one acting like Exalted need a giant pile of Charms to be awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-02T17:11:18-08:00","id":1501990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1501989#post1501989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think most of us don't really expect this approach to the game where you're trying to evenly spread out Charms between all of your Caste and Favored Abilities.<br /> <br /> I'd also point out that given how fast Solar Charm Ability Minimums jump to 4 and 5, most characters aren't going to qualify for all the many Charms between those 10 Abilities because they're not going to worry about getting them all to 5. Most PCs are probably putting the vast majority of their Charms in 2-4 Abilities, with a small smattering in other places. As well, the Solar Charms are generally ones where exploring every last branch really isn't that important.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's like, your opinion, man. Most players I know have AT LEAST 4 abilities at 5 at character creation. And I didn't say every last section of the charm tree. I was just pointing out that the charm trees are DENSE and your idea of only needing 10 or so in 2 trees and a smattering of a few others is EXTREMELY untrue from my short experience in the game.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1501989#post1501989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While there are obvious divisions in some of them, they all have Charm packages that support more specific concepts that mean you don't have to buy every Charm to get what matters to why you picked that Ability as one to focus on.<br /> <br /> With intended groups of 3-6 players, and Solar Charms not really rewarding overlap over diversity, most Charms worth having are going to come up even if one Character doesn't have them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, if you have 6 players in the game I guess some of them might take a lot of bureaucracy charms or heavily invest in investigation. But I doubt it. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1501989#post1501989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? Epic heroes aren't pathetic because they can can cut a mountain in half, but can only throw a knife twice as well as any normal human ever could. Specialization is not a bad thing for the game as it's advised to be played.<br /> <br /> Considering the 6-8 dice + 1 Charm + Excellency is enough for a Solar to beat 90-95% of potential challenges in the setting that Ability addresses, you don't need 20+ Charms to be a powerhouse by the standards of Creation, even if you're still far from the pinnacle of Exalted capabilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why don't you take a look at the base stats on a Tyrant Lizard and let me know if those 6 dice, excellent strike, and the melee excellency are going to win. Just because you can beat the conscript troops doesn't mean anything. The reason you are an Exalted is so that you can face things with slightly more ability, like a Deathlord. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1501989#post1501989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh? I'm treating it as superfluous because by that point a circle of Solars are so powerful you need to beak out every contrived excuse as to why enemies have the power to stand up to them. You're the one acting like Exalted need a giant pile of Charms to be awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prove me wrong. I distinctly remember 2nd edition claiming that 5 essence 5 solars could face the UCS in a fight. I don't see that as happening in this edition. The basic 2nd circle demons in the core beat the hell out of most circles with 20 charm in anything other than melee. There is literally game destroying foes in Exalted and that's who they should be fighting at essence 5. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-02T20:15:26-08:00","id":1501998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1501990#post1501990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's like, your opinion, man.</div> </div> </div> </div>So is everything you're posting dude. But this forum's been talking about all this since 3e came out. There's lots of threads that have exhaustively detailed many of the things we're talking about already.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most players I know have AT LEAST 4 abilities at 5 at character creation. </div> </div> </div>You get that supports what I'm saying right? They're not prioritizing all ten caste/favored equally.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I didn't say every last section of the charm tree. </div> </div> </div>And yet you consistently stress how you can max out every Charm in trees with 52 Charms and still have stuff in others. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was just pointing out that the charm trees are DENSE and your idea of only needing 10 or so in 2 trees and a smattering of a few others is EXTREMELY untrue from my short experience in the game.Sure, if you have 6 players in the game I guess some of them might take a lot of bureaucracy charms or heavily invest in investigation. But I doubt it. </div> </div> </div>The Charm trees might be dense, but the systems they interact with beyond Combat aren't really that dense; even crafting. 10 Charms is actually a lot for Abilities you're not going to use in combat. Having played an Investigation Supernal with a side of Bureaucracy, I think you don't really know what the hell those can do when applied to their linked systems. Investigation's reflexive &quot;detect sus people&quot; Charms backed up with the insane information machine that is Ten Magistrate Eyes, lets you basically just stroll into a place and uncover any major criminal conspiracy going on, and then you can use the Defy Official's Way branch to either help the law or the criminals as you see fit by using your insta-super-investigation to give the organization you side with to operate perfectly thanks to the knowledge of how to root out any internal problems, and know who the biggest external threats are.<br /> <br /> <br /> While he needed his circlemates with more social graces to get people to listen, my character waltzed into a city, discovered a plot to rebel against the city leaders, turned in all the ring leaders, and clean out all of the corrupt officials in the city guard that were either fueling public distrust of the city government or being bought off by the rebels... in basically two days.<br /> <br /> Obviously what your ST puts in front of your matters a lot too.<br /> .<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why don't you take a look at the base stats on a Tyrant Lizard and let me know if those 6 dice, excellent strike, and the melee excellency are going to win. </div> </div> </div>That's the easy part. The only actual scary part about fighting a Tyrant Lizard as a Solar is that Tyrant Lizards have a decent JBA combined with a base 5 Initiative. Use you stunting skills and blow a bunch of motes on JBA to get to equal or better Init as the Tyrant Lizard. Then cheese dual weapon clash attacks. It's a hell of a slog, but Legendary Size actually works against the Tyrant Lizard because you can't crash it, so it can't recover from crash while you're trying to work through its massive Heath boxes. Constantly keeping it as Init 1 while using clashes to maximize your mote efficiency, and you'll be able to keep up a better dice pool that will win the crash roll off the vast majority of the time. It's not 100% sure fire, but the odds are way in your favor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The reason you are an Exalted is so that you can face things with slightly more ability, like a Deathlord. </div> </div> </div>And... have you run into any trouble having a Deathlord BBEG at the end of a long campaign serving that purpose? The books don't advocate starting the game with fighting the Underworld's top ghosts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The basic 2nd circle demons in the core beat the hell out of most circles with 20 charm in anything other than melee. </div> </div> </div>How badly made are your group's PCs? The Core 2nd Circle Demon are no pushovers that you can cheese like the Tyrant Lizard, but their combat stats aren't that good. Even moreso if they try to fight a circle of Solars solo and get slammed by action economy and onslaught penalty issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T04:52:59-08:00","id":1502019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1501990#post1501990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> from my short experience in the game.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This right here, stop theroycrafting it and just play out a campaign or two and seee how it feels at e4+. As i have played to that level more than once and my groups are often running out of charms they are all that interested in and just picking fun little toys or something because they got to pick something. Like by that point most people have their primary and seconday skill set well develop in both Dots and charms and aren't being really challenged in it all. Difinitely never felt weak at that level, groups easily curb stomping and speeding right past like any opposition put in our way regardless of the arena.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5280-gfrobbin84","name":"gfrobbin84","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T11:48:57-08:00","id":1502035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1501998#post1501998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So is everything you're posting dude. But this forum's been talking about all this since 3e came out. There's lots of threads that have exhaustively detailed many of the things we're talking about already.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, in my other thread I've brought this up. I'm assuming I'm just behind on the discussion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1501998#post1501998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You get that supports what I'm saying right? They're not prioritizing all ten caste/favored equally.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you said 2-4. Saying at least 4 is not the same thing as all ten but definitely implies more than two but you can believe what you want.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1501998#post1501998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet you consistently stress how you can max out every Charm in trees with 52 Charms and still have stuff in others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you fucking high? I've consistently said that 3 charms in an ability set is not a good example of power at essence 5. I never said you needed every charm in the tree to be good at exalted. What I said was that there is no way of even remotely getting anywhere near an adequate amount of power in any one ability tree RAW unless you sacrifice every other ability to it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1501998#post1501998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Charm trees might be dense, but the systems they interact with beyond Combat aren't really that dense; even crafting. 10 Charms is actually a lot for Abilities you're not going to use in combat. Having played an Investigation Supernal with a side of Bureaucracy, I think you don't really know what the hell those can do when applied to their linked systems. Investigation's reflexive &quot;detect sus people&quot; Charms backed up with the insane information machine that is Ten Magistrate Eyes, lets you basically just stroll into a place and uncover any major criminal conspiracy going on, and then you can use the Defy Official's Way branch to either help the law or the criminals as you see fit by using your insta-super-investigation to give the organization you side with to operate perfectly thanks to the knowledge of how to root out any internal problems, and know who the biggest external threats are.<br /> <br /> <br /> While he needed his circlemates with more social graces to get people to listen, my character waltzed into a city, discovered a plot to rebel against the city leaders, turned in all the ring leaders, and clean out all of the corrupt officials in the city guard that were either fueling public distrust of the city government or being bought off by the rebels... in basically two days.<br /> <br /> Obviously what your ST puts in front of your matters a lot too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Congrats, you beat up a mortal city with your starter character. Now try that in Great Forks or the Realm where actual competent supernatural threats exist. <br /> .<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1501998#post1501998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the easy part. The only actual scary part about fighting a Tyrant Lizard as a Solar is that Tyrant Lizards have a decent JBA combined with a base 5 Initiative. Use you stunting skills and blow a bunch of motes on JBA to get to equal or better Init as the Tyrant Lizard. Then cheese dual weapon clash attacks. It's a hell of a slog, but Legendary Size actually works against the Tyrant Lizard because you can't crash it, so it can't recover from crash while you're trying to work through its massive Heath boxes. Constantly keeping it as Init 1 while using clashes to maximize your mote efficiency, and you'll be able to keep up a better dice pool that will win the crash roll off the vast majority of the time. It's not 100% sure fire, but the odds are way in your favor.</div> </div> </div> </div> Lol sure dude. Cheese dual weapon clash attacks. This is the lamest version of combat possible on par with persistent defense spam in 1st edition or perfect turtling in 2nd. You haven't helped your argument that &quot;the system is good on it's own&quot; by showing a shit strategy in a bad combat system. Also, pardon me but idk what JBA is other than Join Battle something.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1501998#post1501998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And... have you run into any trouble having a Deathlord BBEG at the end of a long campaign serving that purpose? The books don't advocate starting the game with fighting the Underworld's top ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said start a game that way. I just said that beating up extras with an excellency isn't a good example of power of exalted PCs. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1501998#post1501998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How badly made are your group's PCs? The Core 2nd Circle Demon are no pushovers that you can cheese like the Tyrant Lizard, but their combat stats aren't that good. Even moreso if they try to fight a circle of Solars solo and get slammed by action economy and onslaught penalty issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, I'm pretty sure your investigation supernal would die against a 2nd circle demon, especially if he's the 6 dice and an excellency solar you've been describing. Optimized battle solars are of course going to beat a 2nd circle demon. <br /> <br /> I'm actually happy you are answering these questions with some defensive sass. It makes me optimistic that this edition isn't a total garbage mess that I thought it was. Thanks for putting up with my inexperience.<br /> <br /> Tyzerg<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T11:50:24-08:00","id":1502036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gfrobbin84</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1502019#post1502019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This right here, stop theroycrafting it and just play out a campaign or two and seee how it feels at e4+. As i have played to that level more than once and my groups are often running out of charms they are all that interested in and just picking fun little toys or something because they got to pick something. Like by that point most people have their primary and seconday skill set well develop in both Dots and charms and aren't being really challenged in it all. Difinitely never felt weak at that level, groups easily curb stomping and speeding right past like any opposition put in our way regardless of the arena.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's the point of playing a campaign that long then? Sounds like a waste of time or your ST doesn't know how to scale threats properly.<br /> <br /> Tyzerg","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T13:53:47-08:00","id":1502041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1502035#post1502035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm assuming I'm just behind on the discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not exactly acting like it though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What I said was that there is no way of even remotely getting anywhere near an adequate amount of power in any one ability tree RAW unless you sacrifice every other ability to it. </div> </div> </div>The problem is yous seem to have no idea how powerful Solar Charms really are in the system, and how early you just win against anything that isn't at least a Celestial Exalted or similar in power. And even then, you're going to blow past them in your main specialties pretty fast to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Congrats, you beat up a mortal city with your starter character. Now try that in Great Forks or the Realm where actual competent supernatural threats exist. </div> </div> </div>I don't recall informing you which city it was (because it was homebrew) or what kind of opposition we faced (Dragonblooded and Abyssals mainly, but the thing my PC did was do what the DBs do, but way better: provide order and stability, as he didn't have rival Houses dragging down his system). He didn't &quot;beat up&quot; a city of mortals, he converted a whole city of mortals, and a bunch of DBs along with them, to following his lead by fixing the city's most pressing internal problems and put them in a position to beat a Death Knight army (and yes, with the secret help of four other Solars around to make that work).<br /> .<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is the lamest version of combat possible on par with persistent defense spam in 1st edition or perfect turtling in 2nd. </div> </div> </div>You didn't ask me to make it cool or fun to do.<br /> <br /> The point of the example isn't that it's a great way to play the game, but to illustrate how little investment you need into these things to do be effective. A Supernal Melee Dawn combat heavy isn't going to need to resort to this sort of thing, making it the opposite of 1e and 2e problems: cheese is what low level characters do to ensure victory against things that on paper look like more of a threat. Highly invested characters just plow through these things without it instead of it just getting worse at higher levels.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You haven't helped your argument that &quot;the system is good on it's own&quot; by showing a shit strategy in a bad combat system. </div> </div> </div>When did I say that exactly?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, pardon me but idk what JBA is other than Join Battle something. </div> </div> </div>Action. When you actually roll your Join Battle pool, so it can be improved by Charms/stunts/etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I just said that beating up extras with an excellency isn't a good example of power of exalted PCs. </div> </div> </div>Tyrant Lizards are extras now?<br /> <br /> The point you seem completely unwilling to accept, is that Solars are powerful without needing giant buckets of Charms. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dude, I'm pretty sure your investigation supernal would die against a 2nd circle demon, especially if he's the 6 dice and an excellency solar you've been describing. Optimized battle solars are of course going to beat a 2nd circle demon. </div> </div> </div>1) My Investigation Supernal was fine in combat because he used MA and spent his Solar XP there to make sure he could hold his own in fights. Which you know, goes back to the whole initial thing in the thread. Having a bucket of side XP to make sure you don't one-trick pony yourself is a good thing.<br /> <br /> 2) You seem exceedingly resistant the idea that Exalted is built around the idea that you're going to have a group of PCs. The game isn't built around the idea that a 2nd Circle Demon is going to be fighting one-on-one, but one-on group. One combat heavy that can probably beat the demon solo is going to be backed up by 2-5 more Solars that might have much worse odds against said demon alone, but together it's going to be a curb stomp.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1502036#post1502036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What's the point of playing a campaign that long then? Sounds like a waste of time or your ST doesn't know how to scale threats properly.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Welcome to a regular complaint about the game going back to 1e. Scale threats in Exalted is really hard to do well.<br /> <br /> Of course, the point of the game is that eventually your PCs aren't just a bunch of wandering adventures kicking ass and taking names. They're world changing heroes, and they're supposed to get on to fixing things that require more than hitting it with a magical sword over and over.<br /> <br /> While to mixed success, one of the design ideal of 3e is less Charms that &quot;solve&quot; plot instead of ones that help progress plot. My Investigation Solar might have well just been handed the ST notes of every major NPC's secrets and schemes, but that didn't tell him what to do about it all to achieve his goals. That's what makes higher level Exalted play really interesting over more and more Charms: what your characters do with all that power now that they have it. The game might have all the tools for going full Shonen Battle anime where it's a constant treadmill of getting stronger only to face enemies that push you to your limits so you get stronger again, rinse, repeat, if that's what your group wants. But a lot of people get tired of it that loop and want the stakes of the game to shift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T14:46:31-08:00","id":1502049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1502036#post1502036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What's the point of playing a campaign that long then? Sounds like a waste of time or your ST doesn't know how to scale threats properly.<br /> <br /> Tyzerg</div> </div> </div> </div>Heavy Arms already touched on it pretty well and I don't mean fights aren't still challenging at times and always fun but a group of 4 e4 celestials is really hard to challenge unless you are going up agianst other high essence exalts, but at this point the game is more about trying to solve and prevent a world destroying event instead of what's the next biggest baddy we can find. Exalted, especially Solars, has always been a game more about dealing with the consequences of your success than it is about the threat of failure. My point was without actually playing to a high level you don't realize how easy it is to be strong in your primary focus and a secondary, and by strong I mean most likely will beat anything short of another Celestial exalt of equal power that has invested even more but even then it doesn't mean he will always beat you. As while most of the trees are pretty big most of the work horse charms that do all the cool dice tricks are at e1 and e2, the higher level ones are more specialized and flashy, but will also flare you and empty your mote pools fast even at high essence. So it really only takes a handful of charms in a tree to be incredibly skilled and effective at it, greater investment is just to be flashy and cool or have trump cards for select oppurtunities. This is mine and the groups I have played with experience at least, and I almost never spend Solar XP on MAs or Evocations I love just pumping up my abilities and attributes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5280-gfrobbin84","name":"gfrobbin84","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T06:27:46-08:00","id":1502101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1502041#post1502041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're not exactly acting like it though.</div> </div> </div> </div> Excuse my humble sir, may I, a newly born 3rd edition player, have some advice? I've been playing WW games for 25 years now. I have a pretty good understanding of basic experience point leveling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1502041#post1502041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tyrant Lizards are extras now?<br /> <br /> The point you seem completely unwilling to accept, is that Solars are powerful without needing giant buckets of Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div> No, once again I was referring to the 6 dice and an excellency nonsense you brought up. Then to make your bad argument work, you have to cheese the system to make it work. For those not trying to abuse a bad combat system, my point stands. Because...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1502041#post1502041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) My Investigation Supernal was fine in combat because he used MA and spent his Solar XP there to make sure he could hold his own in fights. Which you know, goes back to the whole initial thing in the thread. Having a bucket of side XP to make sure you don't one-trick pony yourself is a good thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's some munchkin-ing right there and actually helps my point. The only way your character was good in combat was because you abused the system to get combat charms through Solar EXP, which is exactly my point.<br /> <br /> What if I did the same but I wanted Thrown instead of MA?<br /> <br /> You seem exceedingly resistant to the idea that the game doesn't work my way because you cant shit all over it with MA Solar EXP hacks and dual wield clash attack spam. You are hurting your own argument as to why the system is fine as is by showing how you can exploit it. I'm not an exploiter so a lot of your examples would never enter my brain.<br /> <br /> So, I apologize if my understanding of the game isn't based on cheesy munchkin tactics that you are apparently very aware of. Back to my point of not having 10k posts on this forum and being new to the discussion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T16:46:48-08:00","id":1502167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1502101#post1502101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Excuse my humble sir, may I, a newly born 3rd edition player, have some advice?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spare me. If you want to be treated like a serious poster, post like a serious poster. If you want to be treated like a joke, keep going. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've been playing WW games for 25 years now. I have a pretty good understanding of basic experience point leveling. </div> </div> </div>Nobody's questioned that. What you clearly don't have, and have outright admitted is the case, is a deep knowledge of the specific intricacies of Exalted 3e.<br /> <br /> The problems you're talking about aren't in the XP system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, once again I was referring to the 6 dice and an excellency nonsense you brought up. </div> </div> </div>Where did I get any math on it wrong? Where did I go against anything stated in the text about the way the rules are meant to be used? How does this violate the spirit of the game as expressed anywhere in the text?<br /> <br /> It's not nonsense, it's how the game is meant to work. Even something as small as one baseline Solar Charm and the free Excellency you get with it, can turn something from &quot;there's no point in rolling this, the dino is going to easily eat you,&quot; to, &quot;if you fight smart and conserve your resources, you can slog your way to be the favored combatant to win.&quot; I called it cheese before you even had a chance to complain, but then again I also didn't object to your enemy selection either (or add in Artifact weapon stat blocks, or get into how many ways whatever Ability you invested in way more than Melee could have been brought to bare, etc etc etc.). Because it just illustrates that you, again, aren't acting like someone that really thinks they have a lot to learn about how 3e works to understand where the breaking points are in the system and how to actually fix them. You just picked a Tyrant Lizard, assuming that any extremely low level of Solar power couldn't beat it since Solars have bloated Charm trees where you need to invest dozens of Charms to be great at things. <br /> <br /> But that's not how the Solar Charms are busted. A lot of the Essence 1 Charms are some of the best Charms the Solars get The developers called the Solar Charm organization a &quot;helix&quot; because that's actually fairly accurate: they're not a straight line up in power. They start off with some pretty broad utility powers that quickly separate Exalted from things that can't use Essence (and even then put them ahead of plenty of things that can pretty quickly), then they circle back to less overtly status changing stuff for things that are orient around being the best of the best in your area of specialty, then they circle around that space a bit before getting to the &quot;insane displays of power&quot; stuff at the top. The first part of the helix spiral is what puts Solars head and shoulders above the vast majority of stuff in Creation. It means a few Charms and decent stats make them top-tier competitors in whatever that is. The second tier of the spiral is when Solars get ahead of specialist Essence users that aren't Solars, which doesn't really make them any better at squishing lower level stuff because the first tier takes care of that. The third tier, is for taking on the the highest level select few of Creation that can stand up to Solars, and super-magic flexing to plow through things quickly instead of bothering to roll out full fights that you weren't going to lose anyway.<br /> <br /> As noted in the other thread, Solars get messy Charms sets because they go first. Just like every other edition this hit 3e too. Maybe Crucible of Legends will help a bit, maybe it wouldn't we'll see. A lot of the problems with the Solar Charms are the 2nd tier's size. Solar Charms should look more like an hourglass than a helix. There's just a huge amount of cruft and bloat that's all about making sure Solars can one up Terrestrial and Celestial opponents in the same era of specialization, which is a really boring thing to have so many Charms built around. That's why there's so many people that want to fix the Solar Charms (and not all of those make the list that much smaller) instead of just throwing most XP to buy more Charms at the players <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then to make your bad argument work, you have to cheese the system to make it work. For those not trying to abuse a bad combat system, my point stands. </div> </div> </div>You're just goal-post shifting.<br /> <br /> &quot;You can't do X under the following conditions!&quot;<br /> &quot;Sure I can, here watch.&quot;<br /> &quot;No, you can't because A, B, and C conditions I'm making up on the spot weren't met!&quot;<br /> <br /> I used clash attacks for exactly what they're supposed to do: push the fight in my character's favor. If you're stuck in an attrition situation, you need to fight like it. When you get told you can only use the Melee Excellency and one offensive Charm, you're going to use tactics that favor offense, and that's clashing as much as possible (that's explicitly why you try to clash if you do: because you can throw better offenses than your opponent, that's what the combat option is meant to benefit).<br /> <br /> If I was stuck using Dodge instead, would you be complaining if I used a bow, and then Dodge to keep away so I could kite instead? Or do you demand characters fight like idiots for these sorts of hypothetical examples?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's some munchkin-ing right there and actually helps my point. </div> </div> </div>How is using the rules as written and intended (explicitly!) munchkining? You can spend Solar XP on MA specifically to encourage MA as a go to for characters that aren't planning to lean heavy into the main combat Abilities. Munchkining is when you go searching around for loopholes and unexpected synergies to get more bang for your buck than was intended by the game-as-presented. Buying MA Charms with your Solar XP is directly stated as something to do. It's not some powergaming secret... it literally just takes reading the section on what you can buy with Solar XP.<br /> <br /> I didn't abuse the system, I used it exactly how it was intended to be used. Which is why you don't have a point here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What if I did the same but I wanted Thrown instead of MA? </div> </div> </div>Pick stuff that benefits Thrown, like grabbing an appropriate Artifact and use your Solar XP on Evocations instead of Thrown Charms: you get a nifty set of thematic but limited in scope powers, instead of the big old native Thrown tree. Just like using MA instead of taking Brawl.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You seem exceedingly resistant to the idea that the game doesn't work my way because you cant shit all over it with MA Solar EXP hacks and dual wield clash attack spam. </div> </div> </div>I have no idea what &quot;your way&quot; is. You're just spewing buzzwords and claiming it makes a coherent argument. Of course the game doesn't work for you if you insist on not playing the game as intended. You're might as well head to one of the Werewolf forums and complain that it's not &quot;proper&quot; that Ventrue players use their XP breaks on Dominate.<br /> <br /> It's not exploiting the system to use the tools the book gives you how the book tells you to use them.<br /> <br /> And I don't think the game is flawless. I just think you have no idea what the flaws actually are. Clash cheesing isn't a flaw because it's an exploit. It's a flaw because it isn't.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T11:00:01-08:00","id":1502222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1501990#post1501990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why don't you take a look at the base stats on a Tyrant Lizard and let me know if those 6 dice, excellent strike, and the melee excellency are going to win. Just because you can beat the conscript troops doesn't mean anything. The reason you are an Exalted is so that you can face things with slightly more ability, like a Deathlord.</div> </div> </div> </div>When Bureaucracy is an Ability, and an Ability a Solar can inextricably select as their Supernal, I find that the message of the game is that part of how one can face down Deathlords and Primordials and whatever nameless horrors reside in the deepmost trenches of the sea is by being able to organise the supply chain that feeds a force against it to a superhuman degree.<br /> <br /> It appears to me that Exalted has always rested on the assumption that the things that the Chosen face are done so in tandem, such that it is not necessary for each individual one of them to be the combat powerhouse in the event, and I find the fiction consistent in a presentation of some Exalted who are powerful in social or intellectual respects can be threatened by things like mid-tier battle gods.<br /> <br /> I think that matters largely in how a game is played across the board, where different scenes might have different characters take the central focus (indeed, Solar XP has this assumption baked in when people are rewarded for ceding the spotlight to somebody else), and within the context of a single fight scene it can be enough of a contribution to be somebody who helps chip a bit more away from Initiative or throws in things like distract gambits. The event that a character with three Melee Charms ends up needing to face down a tyrant lizard alone seems exceedingly rare, and if it does happen I think the tone and objective of the scene would logically be something other than an epic fight scene. I think there are a few ways for a non-fighter to still feel like an epic hero if you actually have them play to their strengths. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T13:19:32-08:00","id":1502232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1502222#post1502222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When Bureaucracy is an Ability, and an Ability a Solar can inextricably select as their Supernal, I find that the message of the game is that part of how one can face down Deathlords and Primordials and whatever nameless horrors reside in the deepmost trenches of the sea is by being able to organise the supply chain that feeds a force against it to a superhuman degree.<br /> <br /> It appears to me that Exalted has always rested on the assumption that the things that the Chosen face are done so in tandem, such that it is not necessary for each individual one of them to be the combat powerhouse in the event, and I find the fiction consistent in a presentation of some Exalted who are powerful in social or intellectual respects can be threatened by things like mid-tier battle gods.<br /> <br /> I think that matters largely in how a game is played across the board, where different scenes might have different characters take the central focus (indeed, Solar XP has this assumption baked in when people are rewarded for ceding the spotlight to somebody else), and within the context of a single fight scene it can be enough of a contribution to be somebody who helps chip a bit more away from Initiative or throws in things like distract gambits. The event that a character with three Melee Charms ends up needing to face down a tyrant lizard alone seems exceedingly rare, and if it does happen I think the tone and objective of the scene would logically be something other than an epic fight scene. I think there are a few ways for a non-fighter to still feel like an epic hero if you actually have them play to their strengths.</div> </div> </div> </div>This so much this and that is why I love Exalted so much compared to say a game like D&amp;D orr Pathfinder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5280-gfrobbin84","name":"gfrobbin84","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-22T12:46:46-08:00","id":1503697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1502036#post1502036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What's the point of playing a campaign that long then? Sounds like a waste of time or your ST doesn't know how to scale threats properly.<br /> <br /> Tyzerg</div> </div> </div> </div>Many Solar games are run as a sandbox where threat scaling is proportional to how loud the PCs are being about their Exalt status and ambitions because it can be very satisfying and make the game world feel more lived-in.<br /> <br /> This might mean the Dawn Caste has a few confrontations with mortal opposition where the question isn't &quot;can they win?&quot; so much as if they're forced to do anything that's clearly superhuman. They can probably pass as god-blooded as long as they don't dip into peripheral essence but even that makes them <i>interesting </i>in a way that's likely to have long-term consequences.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T13:13:46-08:00","id":1504625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1502167#post1502167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Spare me. If you want to be treated like a serious poster, post like a serious poster. If you want to be treated like a joke, keep going.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, great and powerful arbiter of serious posts, please allow this post to be worthy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1502167#post1502167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody's questioned that. What you clearly don't have, and have outright admitted is the case, is a deep knowledge of the specific intricacies of Exalted 3e.<br /> <br /> The problems you're talking about aren't in the XP system.</div> </div> </div> </div> Fair enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1502167#post1502167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that's not how the Solar Charms are busted. A lot of the Essence 1 Charms are some of the best Charms the Solars get The developers called the Solar Charm organization a &quot;helix&quot; because that's actually fairly accurate: they're not a straight line up in power. They start off with some pretty broad utility powers that quickly separate Exalted from things that can't use Essence (and even then put them ahead of plenty of things that can pretty quickly), then they circle back to less overtly status changing stuff for things that are orient around being the best of the best in your area of specialty, then they circle around that space a bit before getting to the &quot;insane displays of power&quot; stuff at the top. The first part of the helix spiral is what puts Solars head and shoulders above the vast majority of stuff in Creation. It means a few Charms and decent stats make them top-tier competitors in whatever that is. The second tier of the spiral is when Solars get ahead of specialist Essence users that aren't Solars, which doesn't really make them any better at squishing lower level stuff because the first tier takes care of that. The third tier, is for taking on the the highest level select few of Creation that can stand up to Solars, and super-magic flexing to plow through things quickly instead of bothering to roll out full fights that you weren't going to lose anyway.<br /> <br /> As noted in the other thread, Solars get messy Charms sets because they go first. Just like every other edition this hit 3e too. Maybe Crucible of Legends will help a bit, maybe it wouldn't we'll see. A lot of the problems with the Solar Charms are the 2nd tier's size. Solar Charms should look more like an hourglass than a helix. There's just a huge amount of cruft and bloat that's all about making sure Solars can one up Terrestrial and Celestial opponents in the same era of specialization, which is a really boring thing to have so many Charms built around. That's why there's so many people that want to fix the Solar Charms (and not all of those make the list that much smaller) instead of just throwing most XP to buy more Charms at the players</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good point and something I didn't know about when it came to the design scheme.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1502167#post1502167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're just goal-post shifting.<br /> <br /> &quot;You can't do X under the following conditions!&quot;<br /> &quot;Sure I can, here watch.&quot;<br /> &quot;No, you can't because A, B, and C conditions I'm making up on the spot weren't met!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>If you say so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1502167#post1502167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I used clash attacks for exactly what they're supposed to do: push the fight in my character's favor. If you're stuck in an attrition situation, you need to fight like it. When you get told you can only use the Melee Excellency and one offensive Charm, you're going to use tactics that favor offense, and that's clashing as much as possible (that's explicitly why you try to clash if you do: because you can throw better offenses than your opponent, that's what the combat option is meant to benefit).<br /> <br /> If I was stuck using Dodge instead, would you be complaining if I used a bow, and then Dodge to keep away so I could kite instead? Or do you demand characters fight like idiots for these sorts of hypothetical examples?</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't think it's ever explicitly stated in the book that clash attacks are used to help with battles of attrition but that's good to know. I guess I didn't realize how important they could be. Still feels cheesy af. Disengaging as a bow user is very obviously vital to survival. So, no I wouldn't be surprised by that. Dual wielding clash attacks, yes, I was surprised by that level of cheese. I only picked Tyrant Lizards because they seemed mid-level.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1502167#post1502167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is using the rules as written and intended (explicitly!) munchkining? You can spend Solar XP on MA specifically to encourage MA as a go to for characters that aren't planning to lean heavy into the main combat Abilities. Munchkining is when you go searching around for loopholes and unexpected synergies to get more bang for your buck than was intended by the game-as-presented. Buying MA Charms with your Solar XP is directly stated as something to do. It's not some powergaming secret... it literally just takes reading the section on what you can buy with Solar XP.<br /> <br /> I didn't abuse the system, I used it exactly how it was intended to be used. Which is why you don't have a point here.</div> </div> </div> </div>MA and sorcery as &quot;go tos&quot; for characters not planning on leaning into the main combat abilities seems stupid as they are definitely on par with the other abilities. It's just having your cake and eating it too but only if you force your character into being one of those types (MAist or Sorcerer) regardless if it makes sense for your character's backstory. Which is why I brought up Thrown.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1502167#post1502167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pick stuff that benefits Thrown, like grabbing an appropriate Artifact and use your Solar XP on Evocations instead of Thrown Charms: you get a nifty set of thematic but limited in scope powers, instead of the big old native Thrown tree. Just like using MA instead of taking Brawl.</div> </div> </div> </div>Evocations are not on par with MA charms but okay.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1502167#post1502167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no idea what &quot;your way&quot; is. You're just spewing buzzwords and claiming it makes a coherent argument. Of course the game doesn't work for you if you insist on not playing the game as intended. You're might as well head to one of the Werewolf forums and complain that it's not &quot;proper&quot; that Ventrue players use their XP breaks on Dominate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea apparently how the game was intended to be played. I'm sure my stance might resemble yours with a few more years of playing under my belt. But, making every 'non-traditional combat ability' character a MAist or a Sorcerer feels like a bad game. And I'm still talking about Solars in an Exalted forum so idk what the hell you are talking about with vampire complaints in a werewolf forum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1502167#post1502167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not exploiting the system to use the tools the book gives you how the book tells you to use them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Other than the experience chart, I must have missed all these helpful tips on how to play the game &quot;as intended.&quot; <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1502167#post1502167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I don't think the game is flawless. I just think you have no idea what the flaws actually are. Clash cheesing isn't a flaw because it's an exploit. It's a flaw because it isn't.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. Thanks for trying to help me understand even if I can come off as an asshole. I'm just passionate about the game and can get tunnel vision about things that upset me about it. Don't even start with how I feel about Exigents vs. God-blooded lol.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T15:11:22-08:00","id":1504654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1504625#post1504625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it's ever explicitly stated in the book that clash attacks are used to help with battles of attrition but that's good to know. I guess I didn't realize how important they could be. Still feels cheesy af. Disengaging as a bow user is very obviously vital to survival. So, no I wouldn't be surprised by that. Dual wielding clash attacks, yes, I was surprised by that level of cheese. I only picked Tyrant Lizards because they seemed mid-level.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're conflating two related but independent thoughts. Clashing isn't for attrition, it's for going all offense. Going all offense is good for attrition because you don't have to spend anything on defense.<br /> <br /> It also feels like you're getting a bit caught up in the abstractions here. Clash-cheesing is a vital and primordial survival tactic. It's older than humans. It's happening all the time. Almost every human culture has an idiom or adage about it. The problem is that those tend to assume we're the Tyrant Lizard closing on what looks like a light snack: don't back your opponent into a corner.<br /> <br /> When you're fighting to survive, and your only option is win or die because running is off the table? You fight. You fight hard, and you fight cheap. You might be at the disadvantage, but you keep going because they might decide it's not worth it, and if you do nothing you die.<br /> <br /> If you think about any video of someone backing a feral animal into a corner... you're going to see that animal try to clash-cheese: they sit there, puff up, and wait. When the person goes in to grab them? That's when they attack. That's a clash: to offensive moves being pitted against each other.<br /> <br /> Whether the corner is literal or not, that's what the Tyrant Lizard vs. no-so-great-Melee Solar is: the Solar is not in a great tactical situation. The Solar is facing that same situation: make it clear that any time that Tyrant Lizard goes in for a bite, it's going to get stabbed. And it's going to keep getting stabbed until one side falls down, or the Tyrant Lizard goes away.<br /> <br /> So this is a very basic survival situation. The only real oddity is dual-wielding light weapons is better than using a spear because the weapon stat blocks are a major source of iffy design decisions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> MA and sorcery as &quot;go tos&quot; for characters not planning on leaning into the main combat abilities seems stupid as they are definitely on par with the other abilities. </div> </div> </div>I don't think that plays out. MA is diverse, but very resource (esp. XP) intensive and difficult to balance because each style has it's own idiosyncrasies and you have to decide if you want to try to mesh a few together that you can use at the same time, or have to switch between them and hope you have time as situations change. The core Charms are, generally, just going to work. MAs might be better for very specific strategies, but they don't pan out as situations get more diverse. They're great for having one style so you have some decent combat utility, but having to buy a 4 dot Merit, and each MA as its own 5 dot Ability, and then Charms? Mastering a few styles gets really expensive really fast and not really that great compared to other options.<br /> <br /> Sorcery is hard to compare because it operates on such a different part of the game. Combat sorcery is a thing, but it's not throwing ki blasts instead of slashing with your sword. &quot;Basic&quot; attack spells like Death of Obsidian Butterflies are massive area attacks that can create problems for your own side if you're not really careful with them. Things like Wood Dragon Claw are great but... you still need to be able to fight with them with other Abilities to get much use out of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Evocations are not on par with MA charms but okay. </div> </div> </div>Based on what?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But, making every 'non-traditional combat ability' character a MAist or a Sorcerer feels like a bad game. </div> </div> </div>Or an Evocation heavy user too.<br /> <br /> But that's only a big deal if you intend on having a lot of combat and you need non-combat Ability focused characters to have ways to interact with the combat system more readily (which is going to be typical, but not every character). This can go the other way too. A combat heavy can pick up MAs that do a bunch of social effects, or Sorcery that's more utility focused, or Evocations with crazy mystical effects (there's an axe lets you power Sorcery by chopping people with it in one of the books).<br /> <br /> The whole point is that Solar XP helps you branch out in games where branching out it going to be useful. You can also be in a game where you don't want/need that sort of thing, and you can use Solar XP to dump into getting 5s in every last little Attribute and Ability that matters to what you do, and all those Purchase Merits to eke out a few more dice, etc.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T15:49:53-08:00","id":1504667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1504654#post1504654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're conflating two related but independent thoughts. Clashing isn't for attrition, it's for going all offense. Going all offense is good for attrition because you don't have to spend anything on defense.<br /> <br /> It also feels like you're getting a bit caught up in the abstractions here. Clash-cheesing is a vital and primordial survival tactic. It's older than humans. It's happening all the time. Almost every human culture has an idiom or adage about it. The problem is that those tend to assume we're the Tyrant Lizard closing on what looks like a light snack: don't back your opponent into a corner.<br /> <br /> When you're fighting to survive, and your only option is win or die because running is off the table? You fight. You fight hard, and you fight cheap. You might be at the disadvantage, but you keep going because they might decide it's not worth it, and if you do nothing you die.<br /> <br /> If you think about any video of someone backing a feral animal into a corner... you're going to see that animal try to clash-cheese: they sit there, puff up, and wait. When the person goes in to grab them? That's when they attack. That's a clash: to offensive moves being pitted against each other.<br /> <br /> Whether the corner is literal or not, that's what the Tyrant Lizard vs. no-so-great-Melee Solar is: the Solar is not in a great tactical situation. The Solar is facing that same situation: make it clear that any time that Tyrant Lizard goes in for a bite, it's going to get stabbed. And it's going to keep getting stabbed until one side falls down, or the Tyrant Lizard goes away.<br /> <br /> So this is a very basic survival situation. The only real oddity is dual-wielding light weapons is better than using a spear because the weapon stat blocks are a major source of iffy design decisions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, this was actually a really helpful and insightful example. I was thinking of clashing as two samurais cutting each other down but this example makes a lot more sense as to why you would do it. The reach tag should really be more useful than it is for exactly these types of scenarios.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1504654#post1504654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that plays out. MA is diverse, but very resource (esp. XP) intensive and difficult to balance because each style has it's own idiosyncrasies and you have to decide if you want to try to mesh a few together that you can use at the same time, or have to switch between them and hope you have time as situations change. The core Charms are, generally, just going to work. MAs might be better for very specific strategies, but they don't pan out as situations get more diverse. They're great for having one style so you have some decent combat utility, but having to buy a 4 dot Merit, and each MA as its own 5 dot Ability, and then Charms? Mastering a few styles gets really expensive really fast and not really that great compared to other options.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right. I forgot about the individual MA ability dots as well as other complications like form weapons, etc etc. You'd be much better off taking melee 5 and DSD to be fair most of the time. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1504654#post1504654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorcery is hard to compare because it operates on such a different part of the game. Combat sorcery is a thing, but it's not throwing ki blasts instead of slashing with your sword. &quot;Basic&quot; attack spells like Death of Obsidian Butterflies are massive area attacks that can create problems for your own side if you're not really careful with them. Things like Wood Dragon Claw are great but... you still need to be able to fight with them with other Abilities to get much use out of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I was initially irked about Sorcerous motes, etc in general but the more I have my players use sorcery, the less of an issue it is. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1504654#post1504654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on what?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just initial read throughs but evocations seem so hit or miss that I'm not really sure how I feel about them. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1504654#post1504654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or an Evocation heavy user too.<br /> <br /> But that's only a big deal if you intend on having a lot of combat and you need non-combat Ability focused characters to have ways to interact with the combat system more readily (which is going to be typical, but not every character).</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a kung fu game after all lol. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1504654#post1504654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This can go the other way too. A combat heavy can pick up MAs that do a bunch of social effects, or Sorcery that's more utility focused, or Evocations with crazy mystical effects (there's an axe lets you power Sorcery by chopping people with it in one of the books).</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but I feel this is slightly more atypical than I'd expect. But, I could be wrong. I guess I'll see as my player's exp totals get higher and higher.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1504654#post1504654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole point is that Solar XP helps you branch out in games where branching out it going to be useful. You can also be in a game where you don't want/need that sort of thing, and you can use Solar XP to dump into getting 5s in every last little Attribute and Ability that matters to what you do, and all those Purchase Merits to eke out a few more dice, etc.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I just want my players to have the option of branching out to other ability CHARMS, not just ability dots. A combat monkey who wants to explore sailing shouldn't have to get an artifact that gives him sailing evocations or a spell that summons a demon ship. He should be able to buy sail charms. I can see how that could make for issues with balance but RAW it seems like a pretty winding road to get him to Sailing powers when he could have just went straight to sailing charms. Is it really that big of a deal to do without having to hinder his combat monkeyisms by taking away normal experience for something he just wants to try out?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T10:50:49-08:00","id":1504771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1504667#post1504667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking of clashing as two samurais cutting each other down but this example makes a lot more sense as to why you would do it. The reach tag should really be more useful than it is for exactly these types of scenarios.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clash attacks still work for the samurai showdown thing, but basically you need both sides to actually agree to it (you know, like both following bushido and so on). The system is actually really unclear on how much you can force a clash without Charms. Like, if you delay to attack a target on their turn, and they attack, there's a clash. But if they know you're waiting.. that could just full defense and then there's no clash. It's easier with a violent animal that's just trying to kill you because an animal (at least not one with increased intelligence or whatnot) that's trying to spam you with attacks until it wins. <br /> <br /> Now, it's not always a bad option to &quot;agree&quot; to in a duel, esp. with two relatively evenly matched combatants that both have a desire to see who wins: if things are basically turning into a stalemate of trading withering attacks without on side opening up a lead, both sides throwing a decisive attack clash is probably going to change the course of a fight enough to break the tie (the winner just knocking their opponent down to -1 would penalties can help keep a stalemate from happening again). At least until Charms come into things. If both sides want to just figure out a winner, it's a good option and you get that story beat clash attacks tend to evoke most strongly.<br /> <br /> But in most situations it's kind of a silly strategy because in most situations pitting offense vs. offense is clearly more favorable to one side than the other and there's no reason to agree to it.<br /> <br /> Also, the tag that's more of a problem is the two-handed tag (and how that influenced dual-wielding). One of the trade offs for using both your hands with one melee/MA weapon (whether a two-handed weapon or doubling up the same one-handed weapon) is that you have less access to tags (look at all the tags you could have using a whip in your main hand, and a shield in your off hand, and you could still kick someone as an unarmed attack) but a get a bonus to Clashes.<br /> <br /> This then combines with how on the surface the light vs. medium vs. heavy base weapon stats look sensible, but are completely lopsided in play. Mundane heavy weapons in general are just... bad. Low accuracy and low defense means the damage bonus is essentially irrelevant. Whatever extra bit of damage you do is going to be completely overwhelmed by missing more and getting hit more (in some ancient 3e thread someone actually did out a lot of the numbers on this).<br /> <br /> If you're a Solar, this gets even worse. When you look at those Melee Charms, extra damage is very easy to get (and isn't subject to dice-caps inherently), while light weapon's highest accuracy bonus and medium weapon's defense bonus also don't interfere with your dice caps. If you want that clash bonus - esp. for a low investment option - dual wielding lights or mediums makes way more sense with the Solar Charms than relying on a heavy does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just initial read throughs but evocations seem so hit or miss that I'm not really sure how I feel about them. </div> </div> </div>I guess that's fair. The space that Artifacts take up in 3e with Evocations means just the core book set can be a but underwhelming if none of them fit what you're looking for. As we've gotten more examples and more discussions of design topics in other books, it's easier to find an Artifact Evocation list that looks like something you want. Evocations are generally just as powerful as MA Charms, but more focused on a tighter set of themes. Evocations trees avoid them being one-trick-ponies, but they're by far the most focused on the three &quot;universal&quot; power options; you want the right one paired with the right character (which fortunately is part of the fiction in 3e, the Evocations are supposed to be examples even for that specific Artifact, as they can grant different Evocations to different users even if sticking to their themes).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But, I could be wrong. I guess I'll see as my player's exp totals get higher and higher. </div> </div> </div>Expect to see a decent amount of Terrestrial Circle Sorcery as time goes on. It's just... an obnoxiously large package for goodies even for non-sorcerer Exalted to pass up over a long enough period of time, and there are spells for lots and lots of things without locking yourself so tightly into a specific mode like MA and Evocations tend to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I just want my players to have the option of branching out to other ability CHARMS, not just ability dots. </div> </div> </div>They can? But since they need dots in those Abilities to get those Charms too, you can use your Solar XP to buy up some Sail, and then using your normal XP on a Sail Charm dip. This means less of your XP is being diverted from your core focus than it would in previous editions where the XP for your main focus, those Sail dots, and those Sail Charms were all one pool.<br /> <br /> Again though, it's worth remembering that you don't need to buy 5+ Charms to be a decent backup sailor. Sail might have been an off the cuff choice, but it's frequently complained about because it's one of the most ridiculously easy Abilities for Solars to jump from &quot;struggles with highly skilled and well equipped mortals,&quot; to, &quot;easily defeats anything that isn't an aquatic behemoth or an Essence user with an Artifact ship and magically enhanced crew.&quot;<br /> <br /> The game doesn't have a lot of &quot;light exploring&quot; space when it comes to Charms. Charms ramp up pretty fast (esp. against everything that isn't awesome-magic). If you actually want to enjoy some basic naval combat and so on, it's almost better to not get more than Salty Dog Method (a Charm almost every character will want even if they never step foot on a boat). So things like navel hazards and normal pirate ships are actually interesting for a bit.<br /> <br /> Outside of combat esp. most Solar Charms are just, &quot;Oh, you don't have magic? I win.&quot; Even starter Essence 1 Charms. The lowest level lock-picking Charm is literally &quot;you will pick this lock,&quot; and everything more complex about it is how much trouble a magic lock might cause you in the process of opening it.<br /> <br /> This is actually a hidden part of why MA/Sorcery/Evocations being the way they are can make all of this more fun: they work on different designs. You can make an Artifact boat with a bunch of Evocations that aren't just about breaking the navel combat system over your knee harder than you already can with 1-3 Sail Charms. You can jump right into &quot;cool&quot; effects that aren't about winning conflicts directly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T19:18:19-07:00","id":1505404,"title":"","content":"Confirmed - there are a LOT of Solar Charms. Way more than any character needs, even in their area of specialty. The way the trees are designed are more about &quot;finding your joy&quot;; two characters can take somewhat different subsets of the same ability and both be inhumanly effective. Completing a tree isn't really the goal.<br /> <br /> Were all the subtle gradations absolutely necessary? Maybe not in every case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T20:55:15-07:00","id":1505410,"title":"","content":"I think Solar Awareness is probably a good aim for when 3e Solar design works the best. There's a core &quot;trunk&quot; of Charms that's not too big and you can just rush for super senses across the board. You can branch out to fun tricks with specific senses if you want, but you don't have the weird &quot;mergers&quot; like Athletics where if you want some of the top-tier stuff you have to dip into all of the different trees, or the bloated way each Performance branch starts with the same Charm for a different type of art.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T07:33:01-07:00","id":1508443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1505410#post1505410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Solar Awareness is probably a good aim for when 3e Solar design works the best. There's a core &quot;trunk&quot; of Charms that's not too big and you can just rush for super senses across the board. You can branch out to fun tricks with specific senses if you want, but you don't have the weird &quot;mergers&quot; like Athletics where if you want some of the top-tier stuff you have to dip into all of the different trees, or the bloated way each Performance branch starts with the same Charm for a different type of art.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes me wonder if maybe there's room for a tag, here? What if you had &quot;trunk&quot; Charms that were regular XP only, but some &quot;leaf&quot; charms (or the old submodule/repurchase/upgrade tech) could be bought with Solar XP? I feel like that could create some interesting design space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T08:11:04-07:00","id":1508447,"title":"","content":"Eh? I mean hypothetically... but I'm not sure how well that would work even if one were doing a full re-write of the Charm-set. Look at how underwhelming the Eclipse tag is so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T11:02:31-07:00","id":1508461,"title":"","content":"Fair. I guess I was just thinking that some of the otherwise underwhelming highly-situational or dice-trick Charms might fit better if they were sharing space with things like MA, Sorcery, and Traits, rather than competing for resources with your mainline capabilities. Like, if I'm not all that interested in MA/Sorcery, I can use my Solar XP to add some color to my specialty subject, but not to seriously advance.<br /> <br /> Maybe something like &quot;You can spend Solar XP on Charms if you exceed both the Essence and Ability requirements by 2&quot; instead? I dunno. Just spitballing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T12:50:41-07:00","id":1508477,"title":"","content":"I get it's just spitballing, but it just seems unnecessary. Like, you're playing such a long game that you have so much Solar XP that you've bought up every Attribute, Ability, Specialty, and Merit that you can think of, and you have nothing left to spend it on by Evocations/MA/Sorcery, and you refuse to do it for any of those? Is that really something to worry about creating house rules for?<br /> <br /> For any game I can imagine, you're going to be in high Essence and with more than enough Charms to completely dominate your mainline focus. Your normal XP is already going to start dabbling if it hasn't already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T09:10:21-07:00","id":1508532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1475044-solar-experience-and-charms-what-could-go-wrong?p=1502035#post1502035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Are you fucking high?</div> </div> </div> </div><b><span style=\"color:#e74c3c\">Please leave the thread.</span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T04:07:26-07:00","id":1512939,"title":"","content":"The game would be better if Solars had a slower experience progression and less charms in general imo. Especially for combat.<br /> <br /> 25 combat charms is getting to the point where running an advanced combat between a Solar Circle and an enemy Circle is like playing five overlapping games of MtG at once, and getting surprised when it grinds to a slow boring mess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T15:55:15-07:00","id":1513011,"title":"","content":"While 3e Charm design has generally improved from the core book, it's not like the other Exalted don't have similar issues with high end combat, XP progression, and lots of Charms.<br /> <br /> For the most part, the number of Charms mirrors the complexity of the subsystems they interact with (Craft is the notable exception here, but Solar Craft is probably the worst offender here, and things like Solar Lore invent whole new subsystems just for some of their Charms). There's a lot of combat Charms because there's a lot of moving parts in combat for Charms to work on. <br /> <br /> Even Exalted Essence hits this point eventually, despite Universal Charms covering common effects all Exalted end up with, a different advancement method, and much easier to handle NPC stat blocks. There's only so much you can do about that with the core game play style Exalted focuses on. Tweaking XP progression is never going to stop Exalted from generating combat that's slow thanks to PCs trying to juggle a dozen or two powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}